      },
      "worked": "The unfolded curved surface is a sector of radius $s$. Its arc length equals the circumference of the cone's base.\n$$\\begin{align*}l&=2\\pi r\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{l}{s}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{2\\pi r}{s}.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore its area is\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12s^2\\theta\\\\A&=\\frac12s^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi r}{s}\\right)\\\\A&=\\pi rs.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
